Review written to `docs/reviews/python-gaps/pygap-06-helics-time-sync.md` (83 lines).

**7 findings**: 1 critical, 2 high, 2 medium, 2 low.

| Severity | Finding |
|----------|---------|
| Critical | Multi-rate co-simulation broken — HARES unconditionally steps when granted time < requested time, and the fleet's assert is inverted (`granted >= sim_time_s` when HELICS guarantees `granted <= requested`) |
| High | No end-of-simulation handshake — no `request_time(HELICS_TIME_MAXTIME)` call, just disconnects |
| High | No federation termination sentinel detection — runs all remaining timesteps uselessly after another federate crashes |
| Medium | Iterative time mode unsupported and undocumented |
| Medium | No inter-federate timestep validation — 4-min HARES + 5-min grid drifts by 60s/step |
| Low | Zero time-sync logging — no DEBUG/INFO for grants, start, or finalization |
| Low | Single-timestep fallback period of 1.0s is pathologically small for building simulation |
